---
title: Tissue Curation
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

Tissue curation checks tubes into storage boxes. For each tube you scan or
place, NAHPU writes a museum code to `Museum permanent` or `Museum loan` and
the next free cell to `Storage location`, such as `Box 1: D1`. Tubes are
specimen parts and, if you include them, parasites.

Use it when tubes go into museum freezer boxes. Scan each tube as it goes into
the box, and the records match the box with no typing.

